  "question": {
    "text": "The center of mass of a thin rectangular plate (fig - x ) with sides of length $a$ and $b$, whose mass per unit area $(\\sigma)$ varies as $\\sigma=\\frac{\\sigma_0 x}{a b}$ (where $\\sigma_0$ is a constant), would be $\\qquad$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/bGydijWffNDkRTTeUKSXfU73xruwP03ZKOpkAOkKj6c.original.fullsize.png\"/><br/>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "GjrGA",
      "text": "$\\left(\\frac{2}{3} a, \\frac{\\mathrm{~b}}{2}\\right)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "yaOp2",
      "text": "$\\left(\\frac{a}{2}, \\frac{\\mathrm{~b}}{2}\\right)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "nqdp7",
      "text": "$\\left(\\frac{1}{3} a, \\frac{\\mathrm{~b}}{2}\\right)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SEEjX",
      "text": "$\\left(\\frac{2}{3} a, \\frac{2}{3} b\\right)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & d m=\\sigma d A \\\\ & \\begin{aligned} d & =\\sigma(d x)(d y)=\\frac{\\sigma_0 x}{a b}(d x)(d y) \\\\ x_{c o m} & =\\frac{\\int x d m}{\\int d m}=\\frac{\\int x \\frac{\\left(\\sigma_0 x\\right)}{a b}(d x)(d y)}{\\int_0 \\frac{\\sigma_0}{a b}(d x)(d y)} \\\\ & =\\frac{\\int_0^a x^2 d x \\int_0^b d y}{\\int_0^b x d x \\int_0^b d y}=\\frac{2 a}{3} \\\\ y_{c o m} & =\\frac{\\int y d m}{\\int d m}=\\frac{\\int y\\left(\\frac{\\sigma_0 x}{a b}\\right)(d x)(d y)}{\\int \\frac{\\sigma_0 x}{a b}(d x)(d y)}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}$\n$=\\frac{\\int_0^a x d x \\int_0^b y d y}{\\int_0^a x d x \\int_0^b d y}=\\frac{b}{2}$\ni.e., $\\vec{r}_{\\mathrm{com}} \\equiv\\left(\\frac{2 a}{3}, \\frac{b}{2}\\right)$",
    "image": null
  },
